Z||000000||Ronnie||02-27-2001||06:08 PM||||Drove a 87GT today. It dies when stopping, what would the most likely cause maybe be?<BR>It's a 87GT , auto, 2.8<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd ,leather int.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero2_1_3.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||87GTZ34||02-27-2001||08:16 PM||||Does it start back up w/o a problem?  Are there any codes set?  You may need to make sure the check engine light is working first.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ronnie||02-27-2001||08:28 PM||||It's at a car lot. The guy says it has to cool off in order to start back up.We drove it , and it stalled with my wife while turning in another road. We had to wait quite a few mins before it finally started again.He said they would fix it , but was just wondering what might cause this.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Phil||02-27-2001||08:30 PM||||If it idles fine in Park and Neutral but dies in Drive, the problem could be a malfuntioning lock-up solenoid. Diconnect the wires and then drive it a bit to check.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ronnie||02-27-2001||08:48 PM||||Nope. It died in Park when we (finally) got back to the lot. It was idling fine when I parked it, then it just kinda stumbled and choked, about 2 mins later.(if that long)||||reg||6
Z||000005||Ronnie||02-27-2001||08:49 PM||||Guess I should say it's a very nice car , except for this.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Bob Englert||02-27-2001||10:08 PM||||I wonder if the ignition module is on the way out?<P>I guess the thing to do is to try to determine if you are getting spark when it dies.  A heat related problem could be coil, module, or an electrical connection between components.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTZ34||02-28-2001||12:50 AM||||What's the oil pressure like? The reason I ask is because if the fuel pump relay is gone and the oil pressure is on the low side during idle, that will kill the fuel pump and hence pressure.  They (GM) used an oil pressure sender as a backup for the pump relay.  The sitting allows the oil to thicken just enough that it will 'trip' the sender while cranking.  This is how I found out that my fuel pump relay was bad on my 1st Fiero.  With the car off, turn the ignition switch on but don't start it and see if you can hear the fuel pump (see if you hear???). Oh well, you get the idea.  If you don't, most likely the relay is bad.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||02-28-2001||11:59 AM||||87GT, where do I find the fuel pump relay.I didn't think I heard the fuel pump while we were sitting waiting on it to cool down! And it did act like it was getting no fuel, was turning over real good , just wasn't hitting.||||reg||6
Z||000009||87GTZ34||02-28-2001||12:31 PM||||behind the driver in eng compartment. it is attached by a bracket on the firewall.||||reg||1
